"hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1452,"Ubayd Allah bin Saeed bin Kathir bin Ufayr Al-Masry told us, Amr bin Khalid told us, Shihab bin Kharash Al-Hushi told us, Shuaib told me Ibn Ruzaiq Al-Taifi said: I sat next to, or with, a man who was in the company of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called Al-Hakam Ibn Hazan. Al-Kulfi, and he continued to narrate to us, saying: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the seventh of seven, or the ninth of nine, and we witnessed Friday,” so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up, leaning on a bow or a staff, and thanked God and praised Him with mild, kind words. ""Blessings"""
